SC: The photo was taken in Munich, Germany on August 15th, 1945.

INT: Thank you. And can you tell us about this photo, please?

SC: This is the very first photograph that I have of my mother and me taken in Tel Aviv. My mother, Riva Baicovitz. Myself, Shulamit Baicovitz. It was taken in 1946. Probably October 1946.

INT: Thank you. And this photo, please?

SC: This is the very first photo with my father after being reunited in Havana, Cuba. My father, Zalman Baicovitz, and myself, Shulamit Baicovitz, was taken in the American Temple in Havana. I don't know the exact date, but it was sometimes in 1947, February 1947.

INT: Thank you. And these people, who are these people?

SC: Miriam Schulman and myself, Shulamit Baicovitz, taken in Israel in sometimes in 1968.

INT: Thank you. And can you tell us about this photo, please?

SC: My parents, Riva and Zalman Baicovitz and myself, Shulamit, taken on my parents' 50th wedding anniversary August 9th, 1989.

INT: And where was it taken?

SC: In Charlotte, North Carolina.

